* B1 -- Ni2 on coronene
* OpenMolcas: MS-CASPT2 on the QUINTET (S=2) manifold in the
* COMPACT CAS(12,12) active space -- the same active space and the same
* production natural orbitals (rasscf.RasOrb) used by the CASCI
* anchor (03b_exact/cas_ci.input), with MS-CASPT2 treatment.
*
* Comparison to compact CASCI changes correlation treatment at fixed space.
* Comparison to production changes the active-space definition at fixed
* MS-CASPT2 protocol. These are conditional, pathwise sensitivities in a
* three-corner design, not interaction-free method and active-space errors.
*
* CIONLY rebuild reads the converged CAS(26,15) natural orbitals and takes the
* compact 12-orbital window (inactive=100, ras2=12 -> active orbitals 101-112),
* identical to cas_ci.input; CASPT2 settings (imag, IPEA, multistate) are
* identical to the production tier (02_cheap/caspt2_Q.input). The spaces
* are non-nested and the large-space CASCI corner is not calculated.

&GATEWAY
 coord = opt_optimized.xyz
 basis = Def2-TZVP
 group = nosym
 amfi
 RICD

&SEWARD

&RASSCF
 fileorb = rasscf.RasOrb
 cionly
 charge = 0; spin = 5
 nactel = 12 0 0
 inactive = 100
 ras2 = 12
 ciroot = 5 5 1
 thrs = 1.0d-7 1.0d-5 1.0d-5
 outorbital = canonical

&CASPT2
 multistate = 5 1 2 3 4 5
 imag = 0.2
 ipeashift = 0.25
